{"ui_id":"u_000522_01","response_id":"r_000522_01","query_id":"q_000522","intent":"Research Analysis","tags":["health","nutrition","comparative analysis"],"intent_bucket":"research_analysis","genui_json":[{"version":"v0.9","createSurface":{"surfaceId":"surface-leafy-greens-nutrition","catalogId":"https://genui.local/specification/v0_9/standard_catalog.json","theme":{"primaryColor":"#4CAF50"}}},{"version":"v0.9","updateComponents":{"surfaceId":"surface-leafy-greens-nutrition","components":[{"id":"root","component":"Column","children":["header_title","table_container","divider_1","summary_title","summary_text","conclusion_card"]},{"id":"header_title","component":"Text","text":"Nutritional Comparison (per 100g Raw)","variant":"h3"},{"id":"table_container","component":"Column","children":["table_header_row","row_kale","row_spinach","row_chard"]},{"id":"table_header_row","component":"Row","children":["th_green","th_cal","th_vita","th_vitk","th_vitc","th_ca"]},{"id":"th_green","component":"Text","text":"**Green**","variant":"caption","weight":2},{"id":"th_cal","component":"Text","text":"**Kcal**","variant":"caption","weight":1},{"id":"th_vita","component":"Text","text":"**Vit A**","variant":"caption","weight":1},{"id":"th_vitk","component":"Text","text":"**Vit K**","variant":"caption","weight":1},{"id":"th_vitc","component":"Text","text":"**Vit C**","variant":"caption","weight":1},{"id":"th_ca","component":"Text","text":"**Calc**","variant":"caption","weight":1},{"id":"row_kale","component":"Row","children":["td_kale_name","td_kale_cal","td_kale_vita","td_kale_vitk","td_kale_vitc","td_kale_ca"]},{"id":"td_kale_name","component":"Text","text":"Kale","weight":2},{"id":"td_kale_cal","component":"Text","text":"49","weight":1},{"id":"td_kale_vita","component":"Text","text":"500","weight":1},{"id":"td_kale_vitk","component":"Text","text":"389.8","weight":1},{"id":"td_kale_vitc","component":"Text","text":"120","weight":1},{"id":"td_kale_ca","component":"Text","text":"150","weight":1},{"id":"row_spinach","component":"Row","children":["td_spin_name","td_spin_cal","td_spin_vita","td_spin_vitk","td_spin_vitc","td_spin_ca"]},{"id":"td_spin_name","component":"Text","text":"Spinach","weight":2},{"id":"td_spin_cal","component":"Text","text":"23","weight":1},{"id":"td_spin_vita","component":"Text","text":"469","weight":1},{"id":"td_spin_vitk","component":"Text","text":"482.9","weight":1},{"id":"td_spin_vitc","component":"Text","text":"28.1","weight":1},{"id":"td_spin_ca","component":"Text","text":"99","weight":1},{"id":"row_chard","component":"Row","children":["td_chard_name","td_chard_cal","td_chard_vita","td_chard_vitk","td_chard_vitc","td_chard_ca"]},{"id":"td_chard_name","component":"Text","text":"Swiss Chard","weight":2},{"id":"td_chard_cal","component":"Text","text":"19","weight":1},{"id":"td_chard_vita","component":"Text","text":"306","weight":1},{"id":"td_chard_vitk","component":"Text","text":"830","weight":1},{"id":"td_chard_vitc","component":"Text","text":"18","weight":1},{"id":"td_chard_ca","component":"Text","text":"51","weight":1},{"id":"divider_1","component":"Divider"},{"id":"summary_title","component":"Text","text":"Research Summary: Most Beneficial for Bone Density","variant":"h4"},{"id":"summary_text","component":"Text","text":"Based on the values provided, all three leafy greens offer valuable nutrients for bone health, but their contributions differ.\n\nCalcium is a primary structural component of bones, and Kale stands out with the highest calcium content (150 mg per 100g) among the three. Vitamin C is crucial for the synthesis of collagen, which forms the organic matrix of bone, and Kale also provides significantly more Vitamin C (120 mg) than spinach or Swiss chard.\n\nVitamin K plays a critical role in bone metabolism by activating proteins like osteocalcin, which helps bind calcium to the bone matrix. Swiss Chard is exceptionally rich in Vitamin K, offering 830 mcg per 100g, which is substantially higher than both Kale and Spinach. Spinach also provides a significant amount of Vitamin K (482.9 mcg)."},{"id":"conclusion_card","component":"Card","child":"conclusion_layout"},{"id":"conclusion_layout","component":"Column","children":["conclusion_header","conclusion_text"]},{"id":"conclusion_header","component":"Text","text":"Winner: Kale","variant":"h5"},{"id":"conclusion_text","component":"Text","text":"While Swiss Chard provides the highest amount of Vitamin K, **Kale** appears to be the most beneficial for bone density based on this specific set of nutrients. It offers the highest amount of calcium (the direct building block for bones) and Vitamin C (essential for collagen formation), alongside a substantial amount of Vitamin K. This combination makes Kale a strong contender for overall bone health support by contributing to both the mineral density and the structural integrity of bones."}]}}],"assets":[],"toon":"[2]:\n  - version: v0.9\n    createSurface:\n      catalogId: \"https://genui.local/specification/v0_9/standard_catalog.json\"\n      surfaceId: surface-leafy-greens-nutrition\n      theme:\n        primaryColor: #4CAF50\n  - version: v0.9\n    updateComponents:\n      surfaceId: surface-leafy-greens-nutrition\n      components[38]:\n        - component: Column\n          id: root\n          children[6]: header_title,table_container,divider_1,summary_title,summary_text,conclusion_card\n        - component: Text\n          id: header_title\n          text: Nutritional Comparison (per 100g Raw)\n          variant: h3\n        - component: Column\n          id: table_container\n          children[4]: table_header_row,row_kale,row_spinach,row_chard\n        - component: Row\n          id: table_header_row\n          children[6]: th_green,th_cal,th_vita,th_vitk,th_vitc,th_ca\n        - component: Text\n          id: th_green\n          text: **Green**\n          variant: caption\n          weight: 2\n        - component: Text\n          id: th_cal\n          text: **Kcal**\n          variant: caption\n          weight: 1\n        - component: Text\n          id: th_vita\n          text: **Vit A**\n          variant: caption\n          weight: 1\n        - component: Text\n          id: th_vitk\n          text: **Vit K**\n          variant: caption\n          weight: 1\n        - component: Text\n          id: th_vitc\n          text: **Vit C**\n          variant: caption\n          weight: 1\n        - component: Text\n          id: th_ca\n          text: **Calc**\n          variant: caption\n          weight: 1\n        - component: Row\n          id: row_kale\n          children[6]: td_kale_name,td_kale_cal,td_kale_vita,td_kale_vitk,td_kale_vitc,td_kale_ca\n        - component: Text\n          id: td_kale_name\n          text: Kale\n          weight: 2\n        - component: Text\n          id: td_kale_cal\n          text: \"49\"\n          weight: 1\n        - component: Text\n          id: td_kale_vita\n          text: \"500\"\n          weight: 1\n        - component: Text\n          id: td_kale_vitk\n          text: \"389.8\"\n          weight: 1\n        - component: Text\n          id: td_kale_vitc\n          text: \"120\"\n          weight: 1\n        - component: Text\n          id: td_kale_ca\n          text: \"150\"\n          weight: 1\n        - component: Row\n          id: row_spinach\n          children[6]: td_spin_name,td_spin_cal,td_spin_vita,td_spin_vitk,td_spin_vitc,td_spin_ca\n        - component: Text\n          id: td_spin_name\n          text: Spinach\n          weight: 2\n        - component: Text\n          id: td_spin_cal\n          text: \"23\"\n          weight: 1\n        - component: Text\n          id: td_spin_vita\n          text: \"469\"\n          weight: 1\n        - component: Text\n          id: td_spin_vitk\n          text: \"482.9\"\n          weight: 1\n        - component: Text\n          id: td_spin_vitc\n          text: \"28.1\"\n          weight: 1\n        - component: Text\n          id: td_spin_ca\n          text: \"99\"\n          weight: 1\n        - component: Row\n          id: row_chard\n          children[6]: td_chard_name,td_chard_cal,td_chard_vita,td_chard_vitk,td_chard_vitc,td_chard_ca\n        - component: Text\n          id: td_chard_name\n          text: Swiss Chard\n          weight: 2\n        - component: Text\n          id: td_chard_cal\n          text: \"19\"\n          weight: 1\n        - component: Text\n          id: td_chard_vita\n          text: \"306\"\n          weight: 1\n        - component: Text\n          id: td_chard_vitk\n          text: \"830\"\n          weight: 1\n        - component: Text\n          id: td_chard_vitc\n          text: \"18\"\n          weight: 1\n        - component: Text\n          id: td_chard_ca\n          text: \"51\"\n          weight: 1\n        - component: Divider\n          id: divider_1\n        - component: Text\n          id: summary_title\n          text: \"Research Summary: Most Beneficial for Bone Density\"\n          variant: h4\n        - component: Text\n          id: summary_text\n          text: \"Based on the values provided, all three leafy greens offer valuable nutrients for bone health, but their contributions differ.\\n\\nCalcium is a primary structural component of bones, and Kale stands out with the highest calcium content (150 mg per 100g) among the three. Vitamin C is crucial for the synthesis of collagen, which forms the organic matrix of bone, and Kale also provides significantly more Vitamin C (120 mg) than spinach or Swiss chard.\\n\\nVitamin K plays a critical role in bone metabolism by activating proteins like osteocalcin, which helps bind calcium to the bone matrix. Swiss Chard is exceptionally rich in Vitamin K, offering 830 mcg per 100g, which is substantially higher than both Kale and Spinach. Spinach also provides a significant amount of Vitamin K (482.9 mcg).\"\n        - child: conclusion_layout\n          component: Card\n          id: conclusion_card\n        - component: Column\n          id: conclusion_layout\n          children[2]: conclusion_header,conclusion_text\n        - component: Text\n          id: conclusion_header\n          text: \"Winner: Kale\"\n          variant: h5\n        - component: Text\n          id: conclusion_text\n          text: \"While Swiss Chard provides the highest amount of Vitamin K, **Kale** appears to be the most beneficial for bone density based on this specific set of nutrients. It offers the highest amount of calcium (the direct building block for bones) and Vitamin C (essential for collagen formation), alongside a substantial amount of Vitamin K. This combination makes Kale a strong contender for overall bone health support by contributing to both the mineral density and the structural integrity of bones.\"","validation":{"json_parse_ok":true,"schema_valid_strict":true,"schema_valid_lenient":true,"toon_roundtrip_ok":true,"errors":[],"repair_attempts":0,"repair_needed":false},"metrics":{"content_coverage":0.9,"dup_rate":0.31413612565445026,"lint_score":1.0,"output_tokens_toon":568,"output_tokens_json":556,"component_count":38.0,"unique_component_types":5.0,"max_tree_depth":4.0,"avg_tree_depth":1.3157894736842106,"container_to_text_ratio":0.27586206896551724,"information_chunking_score":0.47435043304463687,"ui_modularity_score":0.13157894736842105,"ui_decomposition_score":0.31713263954298665,"actionable_elements":0.0,"action_coverage":1.0,"url_as_text_rate":0.0,"table_pattern_detected":0.0,"table_cell_coverage":0.0,"section_heading_coverage":0.0,"markdown_leakage_rate":0.0,"missing_ids":0.0,"missing_ids_rate":0.0,"dangling_components":0.0,"dangling_components_rate":0.0,"intent_require_table":1.0,"intent_require_actions":0.0,"intent_require_sections":1.0,"intent_table_ok":0.0,"intent_actions_ok":0.0,"intent_sections_ok":0.0,"intent_expectation_pass":0.0,"intent_score":0.0},"gen":{"provider":"gemini","model":"gemini-3-pro-preview","prompt_version":"genui_gen_v1","latency_ms":55690.5360221