Shibuya\\nTheme: Anime Immersion, Pop Culture Icon\\nActivities:\\n  Morning: Journey to Mitaka for a pre-booked visit to the Ghibli Museum. Immerse yourselves in the enchanting world of Studio Ghibli.\\n  Afternoon: Explore Inokashira Park, adjacent to the museum, which features a zoo and boating pond. Travel to Shibuya.\\n  Evening: Experience the famous Shibuya Crossing, visit the Hachiko statue, and explore Shibuya's shops and restaurants.\\nKey Attractions:\\n  Ghibli Museum (Mitaka): A whimsical museum dedicated to the works of Studio Ghibli. IMPORTANT: Tickets must be purchased months in advance.\\n  Inokashira Park: A large, family-friendly park with a zoo, an aquarium, and paddle boats.\\n  Shibuya Crossing: One of the world's busiest intersections, an iconic Tokyo experience.\\nEXAMPLE Estimated Daily Cost (Family of 4): USD 360\\n  Transportation: USD 60\\n  Meals: USD 220\\n  Activities (Ghibli Museum, park entry): USD 80\\n\\nDay 3: Akihabara & Ueno - Anime, Tech, and Science\\nDate: 2025-06-12 (Thursday)\\nNeighborhood: Akihabara, Ueno\\nTheme: Anime Hub, Electronics, Kid-friendly Museums\\nActivities:\\n  Morning: Dive into Akihabara Electric Town. Explore anime and manga shops, electronics stores, and themed cafes. Kids might enjoy the arcades.\\n  Afternoon: Head to Ueno Park. Choose one kid-friendly museum: the National Museum of Nature and Science (interactive exhibits) or the Ueno Zoo.\\n  Evening: Enjoy dinner in Ueno or Akihabara, perhaps trying a themed restaurant in Akihabara.\\nKey Attractions:\\n  Akihabara Electric Town: The center for Japanese anime, manga, video games, and electronics.\\n  National Museum of Nature and Science (Ueno): Features engaging exhibits on science and natural history, including dinosaurs.\\n  Ueno Zoo: Home to pandas and various other animals, a popular choice for families.\\nEXAMPLE Estimated Daily Cost (Family of 4): USD 380\\n  Transportation: USD 50\\n  Meals: USD 230\\n  Activities (museum/zoo entry, arcades): USD 100\\n\\nDay 4: Odaiba - Futuristic Fun and Interactive Wonders\\nDate: 2025-06-13 (Friday)\\nNeighborhood: Odaiba\\nTheme: Interactive Technology, Future Science, Immersive Art\\nActivities:\\n  Full Day: Take the Yurikamome line to Odaiba, a futuristic entertainment hub.\\n  Morning: Visit Miraikan (National Museum of Emerging Science and Innovation) for hands-on exhibits on robotics, space, and technology.\\n  Afternoon: Experience teamLab Planets TOKYO, an immersive digital art museum (reserve tickets in advance). See the life-sized Gundam statue at DiverCity Tokyo Plaza.\\n  Evening: Enjoy dinner with bay views and perhaps a ride on the Daikanransha Ferris Wheel.\\nKey Attractions:\\n  Miraikan (National Museum of Emerging Science and Innovation): Interactive exhibits on cutting-edge science and technology, including ASIMO robot demonstrations.\\n  teamLab Planets TOKYO: A highly immersive digital art experience that engages all senses.\\n  Gundam Base Tokyo (DiverCity Tokyo Plaza): See the impressive life-sized Gundam statue and explore the official shop.\\nEXAMPLE Estimated Daily Cost (Family of 4): USD 420\\n  Transportation: USD 60\\n  Meals: USD 240\\n  Activities (Miraikan, teamLab, Gundam): USD 120\\n\\nDay 5: Asakusa & Tokyo Station - Traditional Charm and Character Goods\\nDate: 2025-06-14 (Saturday)\\nNeighborhood: Asakusa, Tokyo Station\\nTheme: Traditional Culture, Japanese Characters, Souvenirs\\nActivities:\\n  Morning: Explore Asakusa. Visit Senso-ji Temple, Tokyo's oldest temple, and stroll through Nakamise-dori market for traditional snacks and souvenirs.\\n  Afternoon: Travel to Tokyo Station and explore Tokyo Character Street, an underground mall filled with official shops for popular Japanese characters (Pokemon, Studio Ghibli, Sanrio, Jump Shop, etc.).\\n  Evening: Optional: Ascend Tokyo Skytree for a final breathtaking view of the city. Enjoy a farewell dinner.\\nKey Attractions:\\n  Senso-ji Temple (Asakusa): Tokyo's oldest temple, offering a glimpse into traditional Japan.\\n  Nakamise-dori Market (Asakusa): A lively shopping street leading to Senso-ji, perfect for souvenirs.\\n  Tokyo Character Street (Tokyo Station): A haven for fans of Japanese anime and manga characters.\\n  Tokyo Skytree (Optional): One of the tallest structures in the world, with observation decks.\\nEXAMPLE Estimated Daily Cost (Family of 4): USD 390\\n  Transportation: USD 50\\n  Meals: USD 230\\n  Activities (temple free, shopping, Skytree optional): USD 110\\n\\nGeneral Travel Tips for Tokyo:\\n- Transportation: Purchase a Suica or Pasmo IC card for easy tap-and-go travel on all trains and subways. Children aged 6-11 can get child IC cards at half price.\\n- Food: Be adventurous! Tokyo offers incredible food for all budgets, from convenience store snacks to Michelin-starred restaurants. Many places have kid-friendly options.\\n- Internet: Consider renting a pocket Wi-Fi device or purchasing a local SIM card for constant connectivity.\\n- Language: While many signs are in English, learning a few basic Japanese phrases (hello, thank you, excuse me) is appreciated.\\n- Cash: While cards are accepted in many places, it's wise to carry some cash, especially for smaller shops or street vendors.\\n\\nEXAMPLE Daily Cost Summary (Family of 4, USD)\\n\\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nDay       | Neighborhood      | Transportation | Meals   | Activities | Total\\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nDay 1     | Shinjuku          | 50             | 200     | 70         | 320\\nDay 2     | Mitaka, Shibuya   | 60             | 220     | 80         | 360\\nDay 3     | Akihabara, Ueno   | 50             | 230     | 100        | 380\\nDay 4     | Odaiba            | 60             | 240     | 120        | 420\\nDay 5     | Asakusa, Tokyo St.| 50             | 230     | 110\"\n          variant: body","validation":{"json_parse_ok":true,"schema_valid_strict":true,"schema_valid_lenient":true,"toon_roundtrip_ok":true,"errors":["fallback_generated"],"repair_attempts":1,"repair_needed":true},"metrics":{"content_coverage":1.0,"dup_rate":0.010752688172043012,"lint_score":1.0,"output_tokens_toon":1083,"output_tokens_json":1078,"component_count":2.0,"unique_component_types":2.0,"max_tree_depth":2.0,"avg_tree_depth":1.5,"container_to_text_ratio":1.0,"information_chunking_score":0.0,"ui_modularity_score":0.0,"ui_decomposition_score":0.2833333333333333,"actionable_elements":0.0,"action_coverage":1.0,"url_as_text_rate":1.0,"table_pattern_detected":0.0,"table_cell_coverage":0.0,"section_heading_coverage":0.0,"markdown_leakage_rate":0.14615384615384616,"missing_ids":0.0,"missing_ids_rate":0.0,"dangling_components":0.0,"dangling_components_rate":0.0,"intent_require_table":1.0,"intent_require_actions":1.0,"intent_require_sections":1.0,"intent_table_ok":0.0,"intent_actions_ok":1.0,"intent_sections_ok":0.0,"intent_expectation_pass":0.0,"intent_score":0.3333333333333333},"gen":{"provider":"gemini","model":"gemini-3-pro-preview","prompt_version":"genui_gen_v1","latency_ms":69376.3644695282,"input_tokens":16149,"output_tokens":4760,"cost_usd":null,"error":null},"created_at":"2026-02-07T17:03:42.310143Z"}
{"ui_id":"u_000642_01","response_id":"r_000642_01","query_id":"q_000642","intent":"Travel","tags":["packing-list","adventure","nepal"],"intent_bucket":"travel","genui_json":[{"version":"v0.9","createSurface":{"surfaceId":"ebc_packing_list_surface","catalogId":"https://genui.local/specification/v0_9/standard_catalog.json","theme":{"primaryColor":"#0055A4","agentDisplayName":"TrekGuide"}}},{"version":"v0.9","updateComponents":{"surfaceId":"ebc_packing_list_surface","components":[{"id":"root","component":"Column","children":["header","assumptions_card","category_tabs"]},{"id":"header","component":"Text","text":"Everest Base Camp Trek Packing List (October)","variant":"h1"},{"id":"assumptions_card","component":"Card","child":"assumptions_content"},{"id":"assumptions_content","component":"Column","children":["assumptions_title","assumptions_text"]},{"id":"assumptions_title","component":"Text","text":"Assumptions","variant":"h3"},{"id":"assumptions_text","component":"Text","text":"• The trek is 10 days on the trail.\n• A porter will carry your main luggage (duffel bag).\n• Staying in teahouses (no tent needed).\n• Temperatures: 15°C day / -10°C night.","variant":"body"},{"id":"category_tabs","component":"Tabs","tabs":[{"title":"Clothing","child":"clothing_list"},{"title":"Gear","child":"gear_list"},{"title":"Hygiene","child":"hygiene_list"},{"title":"First-Aid","child":"first_aid_list"}]},{"id":"clothing_list","component":"Column","children":["cloth_1","cloth_2","cloth_3","cloth_4","cloth_5","cloth_6","cloth_7","cloth_8","cloth_9","cloth_10"]},{"id":"cloth_1","component":"Text","text":"**Base Layers (2-3 sets)**\n• Lightweight, moisture-wicking thermal tops and bottoms (merino wool or synthetic)."},{"id":"cloth_2","component":"Text","text":"**Mid Layers (2-3 items)**\n• Fleece jacket (200-300 weight).\n• Light down jacket or synthetic insulated jacket."},{"id":"cloth_3","component":"Text","text":"**Outer Layers (1-2 items)**\n• Waterproof and windproof shell jacket (Gore-Tex or similar).\n• Warm down jacket (600-800 fill power) for evenings."},{"id":"cloth_4","component":"Text","text":"**Trekking Pants (2 pairs)**\n• Durable, quick-drying trekking trousers.\n• Fleece-lined or warm trekking pants for colder days."},{"id":"cloth_5","component":"Text","text":"**Warm Trousers/Fleece Pants (1 pair)**\n• For evenings at teahouses."},{"id":"cloth_6","component":"Text","text":"**Underwear (5-7 pairs)**\n• Moisture-wicking, comfortable."},{"id":"cloth_7","component":"Text","text":"**Socks (5-6 pairs)**\n• Wool or synthetic trekking socks.\n• Liner socks."},{"id":"cloth_8","component":"Text","text":"**Gloves (2 pairs)**\n• Thin liner gloves.\n• Warm, waterproof outer gloves or mittens."},{"id":"cloth_9","component":"Text","text":"**Headwear (2-3 items)**\n• Warm wool or fleece beanie/hat.\n• Sun hat or cap.\n• Neck gaiter or buff."},{"id":"cloth_10","component":"Text","text":"**Sleepwear**\n• Can use a clean set of base layers."},{"id":"gear_list","component":"Column","children":["gear_1","gear_2","gear_3","gear_4","gear_5","gear_6","gear_7","gear_8","gear_9"]},{"id":"gear_1","component":"Text","text":"**Backpacks**\n• Large duffel bag (80-100L) for porter.\n• Daypack (25-35L) for daily essentials."},{"id":"gear_2","component":"Text","text":"**Sleeping Bag**\n• Rated to at least -10°C (comfort)."},{"id":"gear_3","component":"Text","text":"**Footwear**\n• Sturdy, waterproof trekking boots.\n• Camp shoes, sandals, or crocs."},{"id":"gear_4","component":"Text","text":"**Trekking Poles**\n• Highly recommended for stability."},{"id":"gear_5","component":"Text","text":"**Water Storage**\n• 2 x 1L Nalgene bottles.\n• Hydration reservoir (2-3L)."},{"id":"gear_6","component":"Text","text":"**Headlamp**\n• With fresh batteries and spare set."},{"id":"gear_7","component":"Text","text":"**Eyewear**\n• High-quality sunglasses (Category 3 or 4)."},{"id":"gear_8","component":"Text","text":"**Electronics**\n• Power bank, Camera, Phone, Universal adapter."},{"id":"gear_9","component":"Text","text":"**Miscellaneous**\n• Towel, Padlock, Dry bags, Book, Map, Thermos, Snacks, Shopping bag."},{"id":"hygiene_list","component":"Column","children":["hyg_1","hyg_2","hyg_3","hyg_4","hyg_5","hyg_6","hyg_7","hyg_8"]},{"id":"hyg_1","component":"Text","text":"**Toiletries**\n• Toothbrush, paste, biodegradable soap, deodorant."},{"id":"hyg_2","component":"Text","text":"**Hand Sanitizer**\n• Essential for hygiene."},{"id":"hyg_3","component":"Text","text":"**Wet Wipes**\n• For sponge baths or cleaning."},{"id":"hyg_4","component":"Text","text":"**Sun Protection**\n• High SPF sunscreen, Lip balm with SPF."},{"id":"hyg_5","component":"Text","text":"**Toilet Paper**\n• Small roll."},{"id":"hyg_6","component":"Text","text":"**Moisturizer**\n• For face and hands."},{"id":"hyg_7","component":"Text","text":"**Personal Medications**\n• Prescriptions."},{"id":"hyg_8","component":"Text","text":"**Feminine Hygiene**\n• As needed."},{"id":"first_aid_list","component":"Column","children":["fa_1"]},{"id":"fa_1","component":"Text","text":"**Basic Pain Relief**\n• Ibuprofen"}]}}],"assets":[],"toon":"[2]:\n  - version: v0.9\n    createSurface:\n      catalogId: \"https://genui.local/specification/v0_9/standard_catalog.json\"\n      surfaceId: ebc_packing_list_surface\n      theme:\n        agentDisplayName: TrekGuide\n        primaryColor: #0055A4\n  - version: v0.9\n    updateComponents:\n      surfaceId: ebc_packing_list_surface\n      components[39]:\n        - component: Column\n          id: root\n          children[3]: header,assumptions_card,category_tabs\n        - component: Text\n          id: header\n          text: Everest Base Camp Trek Packing List (October)\n          variant: h1\n        - child: assumptions_content\n          component: Card\n          id: assumptions_card\n        - component: Column\n          id: assumptions_content\n          children[2]: assumptions_title,assumptions_text\n        - component: Text\n          id: 